IV. THE CONDITIONAL PUBLIC S-1 DILEMMA: MATERIALIZED RISK VS. FIDUCIARY LOCKOUT

Because the 261-page Form S-1 remains non-public prior to its official EDGAR flip, institutional risk committees and lead underwriters (Morgan Stanley, Goldman Sachs, JPMorgan Chase, Citigroup) face a deterministic, two-pronged legal dilemma under Section 11 of the Securities Act of 1933 (15 U.S.C. § 77k) and Regulation S-K Item 105 upon public effectiveness:

```
